  "result": "Done! All 319 tests pass. Bulk discount successfully implemented:\n\n**Modified src/totals.js - lineDiscount function**:\n- Calculates first discount (line discountPercent or tier discount)\n- For qty \u2265 10, applies additional 2.5% off on amount after first discount\n- Formula: `totalDiscount = firstDiscount + (amountAfterFirstDiscount \u00d7 2.5 / 100)`\n- Bulk discount applies regardless of line discount (even if line has discountPercent: 0)\n\n**How it works**:\n- Example: 10 units @ \u20ac100, 10% line discount, 21% VAT\n  - lineTotal = \u20ac1,000\n  - firstDiscount = \u20ac100\n  - amountAfterFirst = \u20ac900\n  - bulkDiscount = \u20ac22.50 \u2192 \u20ac22 (rounded)\n  - totalDiscount = \u20ac122\n  - vatBase = \u20ac878\n  - vat = \u20ac184\n  - total = \u20ac1,000 - \u20ac122 + \u20ac184 = \u20ac1,062\n\n**Automatic integration**:\n- `lineVat` uses `lineDiscount` \u2192 automatically accounts for bulk discount\n- `invoiceTotals` sums line discounts \u2192 bulk discount included in discount field\n- VAT calculated correctly on amount after both discounts\n\n**Tests added** (17 new, in test/totals.test.js):\n- Bulk discount only for qty \u2265 10\n- Bulk applied after line/tier discount\n- Applied even with no line discount\n- Integer cent calculations\n- Edge cases (exactly 10 units, large quantities)\n- Multiple lines with and without bulk\n\n**Existing tests updated** (in test/invoices.test.js):\n- Tests using qty \u2265 10 now account for bulk discount\n- Formula checks updated to include discount term\n- Hardcoded values replaced with function calls",
